title: LSP Inlay Hints - (Example)

\procedure lsp.ih.pair(a, b:"B") a=<<a>> b=<<b>>
\define lsp.ih.macro(a, b) a=$a$ b=$b$
\function lsp.ih.fn(a, b) [<a>addsuffix<b>]

Open this tiddler's `.tid` file in your editor. Each line says which labels should appear, and renders what the wiki binds:

* <<lsp.ih.pair "x" "y">>: `a:` before `"x"`, `b:` before `"y"`
* <<lsp.ih.pair a:"x" "y">>: no label, since a procedure would give `"y"` to `a`, which is already named
* <<lsp.ih.macro a:"x" "y">>: `b:` before `"y"`, the next parameter left over
* {{{ [lsp.ih.fn[x],[y]] }}}: `a:` and `b:` before the operands
* <<list-links "[tag[LSP Capabilities]]">>: `filter:` before the filter

